# recipe.gustale.com (SINGULAR) — the common typo for recipes.gustale.com
#
# Added 2026-11-12. A 301 to the recipes site.
#
# THE DNS SITUATION (read this before changing anything)
# ----------------------------------------------------
# At the time of writing, recipe.gustale.com has an A record pointing at
# 15.197.162.184 -- NOT at this VPS (62.72.7.218). That address is a
# registrar's URL-redirect service, which already answers with:
#
#     HTTP/1.1 301 Moved Permanently
#     Location: https://recipes.gustale.com
#
# So the singular host already redirects, and it did so before any of
# this. What the registrar's redirect does NOT do is preserve the path:
#
#     recipe.gustale.com/dishes/bakso/   ->  https://recipes.gustale.com/
#     recipe.gustale.com/families        ->  https://recipes.gustale.com/
#
# Every deep link collapses onto the homepage.
#
# THE PLAN
# --------
# 1. The owner changes the A record for recipe.gustale.com to
#    62.72.7.218. Until that happens this block is dormant -- Caddy
#    never sees the host.
# 2. Caddy picks up the host, obtains a certificate for it, and serves
#    the 301 itself -- WITH the path preserved.
# 3. At cutover, the target of the redirect changes from
#    recipes.gustale.com to whatever is canonical then (it is already
#    recipes.gustale.com, so this may not need to change at all).
#
# WHY SERVE IT OURSELVES RATHER THAN LEAVING IT AT THE REGISTRAR
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Two reasons, one of which only matters after the cutover.
#
# - The path. A registrar redirect drops it. A shared link of the form
#   recipe.gustale.com/dishes/bakso/ should land on the dish, not the
#   homepage. Links get shortened and pasted, and people type the
#   singular form.
# - Control. The registrar's redirect target is set in the registrar's
#   panel. At cutover the canonical recipes host changes. If the
#   redirect lives in the registrar it has to be remembered, updated,
#   and verified separately from the deploy -- a second place for the
#   cutover to go wrong, at exactly the moment when the redirect
#   matters most.
#
# PATH PRESERVATION
# -----------------
# `redir` rewrites the host and keeps the path and query string:
#
#     recipe.gustale.com/dishes/bakso/   ->  https://recipes.gustale.com/dishes/bakso/
#
# Caddy's `redir` with a host replacement does this by default. The
# explicit `{uri}` is not needed and would drop the query string.

recipe.gustale.com {
	redir https://recipes.gustale.com{uri} permanent
}
